      "sequences": 10,
      "shots_per_sequence": 500,
      "cycle": {
        "single_qubit": [
          "sx",
          "sy",
          "sw"
        ],
        "no_repeat_per_qubit": true,
        "entangler": "cz",
        "pairs": "coupling_map"
      },
      "ideal_probabilities": "statevector",
      "seeded_by": "run seed"
    },
    "description": "Random circuits generated by the runtime (T10 §5): every cycle gives each qubit a random single-qubit gate drawn from {√X, √Y, √W}, never repeating the previous one on that qubit, then applies cz on the coupled pair; F_XEB = d·⟨p_U(x)⟩ − 1 by (5.1) decays as p^depth. There is no source program: the circuits must differ per sequence and the estimator needs the ideal p_U(x) of each one from the state-vector backend, neither of which a fixed OpenQASM file can express (SPEC_DEVIATIONS.md #41)."
  }
